garithm of SdO (Sum of dO E-states). Many features, like SdO, may follow skewed distributions. Applying a logarithmic transformation normalizes the range, making the feature distribution closer to Gaussian.\n# Usefulness: A normalized SdO value might better contribute to downstream classification models by improving linear relationships, especially since SdO seems to have a wide range and high standard deviation indicating non-normality.\n\ndf['log_SdO'] = df['SdO'].replace(0, 1e-6).apply(np.log)  # Replace 0 values to avoid issues with log(0)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Step 3: Count-based groupings - Frequency of halogens and nitro groups\n# Feature description: Adds a new feature as the sum of the number of halogen atoms (nX) and aromatic nitro groups (nArNO2). Both features relate to the composition of chemicals, and their cumulative influence could play a role in determining biodegradability.\n# Usefulness: The presence of halogens and nitro groups captures key chemical groups known to influence persistence and degradation, especially in biodegradability studies.\n\ndf['halogen_nitro_sum'] = df['nX'] + df['nArNO2']\n```end\n\n### Drops Non-informative or Redundant Features ###\n```python\n# Explanation why the column nCRX3 is dropped\n# nCRX3 (Number of CRX3) has a very low mean (0.0363) and zero median, indicating that the majority of data instances have its value as 0.\ndf.drop(columns=['nCRX3'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column nN-N is dropped\n# nN-N (Number of N hydrazines) has an extremely low mean of 0.0079 and a mode of 0, indicating that this feature does not provide meaningful variation to the dataset.\ndf.drop(columns=['nN-N'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column F01[N-N] is dropped\n# F01[N-N] (Frequency of N-N at topological distance 1) shows a mean of 0.0474 and zero at Q1, Median, and Q3, indicating that the majority of chemicals do not have this feature. It adds minimal discrimination power for the classification task.\ndf.drop(columns=['F01[N-N]'], inplace=True)\n```end"]
